From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orchard migration <noreply@orchardlinux>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:39:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: Add Apple Tristar Lightning charging

iBoot leaves the PMIC input-current limit at 100 mA, which does not
even cover an idle system. Identify the attached source and grant what
it advertises, up to the board maximum:

- USB-C cables: the CC level on the orientation-selected lane, read
  through the Tristar mux and the PMIC ADC (1.5 A or 3 A);
- USB-A cables: the Apple BrickID divider on D+/D-, on both mux banks;
- anything else (computers, hubs, generic chargers): 500 mA, what a
  USB 2.0 port provides.

The capability frame that tells the cable types apart follows the
Tristar firmware's decoder. Unplugging does not reset the limit, so
every PMU event interrupt drops a grant to 500 mA before the events are
attributed; ADC completion and USB endpoint events are benign, anything
else starts a new identification. Grants ramp in 500 mA steps and stay
inside battery temperature, voltage and current limits.

Measured on an iPad 6 with an out-of-tree prototype of this logic:
withdrawal within 1 ms of every unplug, and correct grants for a USB-A
power bank, a Mac hub, an Apple 140 W USB-C charger in both orientations
and a Mac USB-C port.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/Kconfig                 |   16 +
 drivers/power/supply/Makefile                |    1 +
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 1039 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1056 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c

